WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
Murder is a crime.

2
00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:04.570
It also breaks one of
the Ten Commandments.

3
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.340
But lying to a friend
breaks no law in the UK.

4
00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:11.100
Many believers would still call it a sin.

5
00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:14.600
And what about someone who steals
food because they are poor?

6
00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.180
Should they be punished?

7
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.810
So why do people commit crimes?

8
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:22.470
And is breaking the law always
the same as doing wrong?

9
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.660
In this mission, you'll
sort wrongs into crimes,

10
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.950
sins, or both, and weigh
up reasons on each side.

11
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.740
Then you'll read how Jesus answered the
men who brought him a woman caught in

12
00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:35.040
adultery.

13
00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:38.600
Your mission: find out
why people break the law,

14
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.250
and whether breaking it
is always doing wrong.
